{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_511356ffcc4b89c737077bcdfccfd5037b093cdb999c68b093d09fcc84c3cc65"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI includes setup and doctor subcommands for configuring the API key and checking configuration health, plus an mcp subcommand (e.g. hex mcp add, hex mcp list) for managing MCP servers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b13bdb3ed4a3af9da7c5ab5f17f713f2fa8c0dc55fff2e72c149c9d722052e9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Hex offers three modes: non-interactive print mode (e.g. hex --print with optional JSON output), an interactive TUI launched by running hex, and resume via --continue or --resume <id>."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8429bb805ee79bfe1985b9ccaa58782a09902fd6f844d4144d35d3920d467e2c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The codebase is organized into cmd/hex (CLI entry and mode routing), internal/core (Anthropic HTTP client, SSE streaming, types, config), internal/ui (Bubbletea TUI), internal/storage (SQLite persistence), and internal/tools (tool registry and executor)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_908a6d1bc938d7c975a4c56895954e886984af121547d45510ff0956c67e58b8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Conversations persist in SQLite at ~/.hex/hex.db using a hybrid schema (normalized conversations/messages tables plus JSON columns for tool_calls and metadata), with WAL mode, foreign keys, embedded migrations, and resume support."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a74bef5b7f779018d63c022a590307ab8bc2be926572815406f10b5e27fa60d1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool system uses a registry plus executor pattern; tools implement a Go interface with Name, Description, Execute, and RequiresApproval methods, and the executor handles approval callbacks and parameter validation."}],"claim_ids":["clm_511356ffcc4b89c737077bcdfccfd5037b093cdb999c68b093d09fcc84c3cc65","clm_6b13bdb3ed4a3af9da7c5ab5f17f713f2fa8c0dc55fff2e72c149c9d722052e9","clm_8429bb805ee79bfe1985b9ccaa58782a09902fd6f844d4144d35d3920d467e2c","clm_908a6d1bc938d7c975a4c56895954e886984af121547d45510ff0956c67e58b8","clm_a74bef5b7f779018d63c022a590307ab8bc2be926572815406f10b5e27fa60d1"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:48Z","created_by_operation":"op_6ee55452f1224fe8a873a7397394f5ff","id":"pg_163dcdc2728d5b418a47cdd38be95a79","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/2389-research-hex-docs-architecture-md-199a60df68f6-cdd38be95a79.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9ac10410c80a53a49ace2b06c6fb05fa"],"title":"2389-research/hex/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md @ 199a60df68f6","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:48Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6ee55452f1224fe8a873a7397394f5ff"}
